[[:db/retract 17592186100371 :answer-field/choices 17592186100372] [:db/retract 17592186100371 :answer-field/choices 17592186100373] [:db/retract 17592186100371 :answer-field/choices 17592186100374] [:db/retract 17592186100371 :answer-field/choices 17592186100375] [:db/retract 17592186100371 :answer-field/choices 17592186100376] {:db/id 17592186100816 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cc39d04c-8fc6-5458-bd77-d57b514616c4" "question-814f2ed7-2079-5a15-870f-7b1832892ba3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100818 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d724ae77-2273-56ab-852e-2415e473e7f8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cc39d04c-8fc6-5458-bd77-d57b514616c4" :question/id #uuid "cc39d04c-8fc6-5458-bd77-d57b514616c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-13822" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{1}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3x}\\cdot 3=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-edd22d9f-f6c6-5c79-8b35-f5d0306c51e3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-edd22d9f-f6c6-5c79-8b35-f5d0306c51e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "edd22d9f-f6c6-5c79-8b35-f5d0306c51e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d129af00-45fd-56b1-bfbc-bbc2b9c9a339" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d129af00-45fd-56b1-bfbc-bbc2b9c9a339" "answer-0cdc4e41-1390-58a2-bac1-3d5ad6ed32e0" "answer-383da31d-fae5-528c-b771-c06390c58c47" "answer-9a132687-cf9b-5e12-8918-cb54c98b6670" "answer-e2371163-1bcf-5101-ab68-2260fe787c84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d129af00-45fd-56b1-bfbc-bbc2b9c9a339" :answer/id #uuid "d129af00-45fd-56b1-bfbc-bbc2b9c9a339" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cdc4e41-1390-58a2-bac1-3d5ad6ed32e0" :answer/id #uuid "0cdc4e41-1390-58a2-bac1-3d5ad6ed32e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-383da31d-fae5-528c-b771-c06390c58c47" :answer/id #uuid "383da31d-fae5-528c-b771-c06390c58c47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a132687-cf9b-5e12-8918-cb54c98b6670" :answer/id #uuid "9a132687-cf9b-5e12-8918-cb54c98b6670" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2371163-1bcf-5101-ab68-2260fe787c84" :answer/id #uuid "e2371163-1bcf-5101-ab68-2260fe787c84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-814f2ed7-2079-5a15-870f-7b1832892ba3" :question/id #uuid "814f2ed7-2079-5a15-870f-7b1832892ba3" :question/math-academy-id "q-210748" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{u} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a0f12e38-1619-5468-ac12-872947123f4a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a0f12e38-1619-5468-ac12-872947123f4a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0f12e38-1619-5468-ac12-872947123f4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dac76dc6-a248-5bf4-bc16-bc99e472f0d0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-83e83f58-9225-53a6-8e6a-f42f69406481" "answer-be58a7fb-a086-5860-ad30-dd1c817fbd59" "answer-51f5ec9c-cf1f-5d72-a5d8-f8dc65eacd30" "answer-dac76dc6-a248-5bf4-bc16-bc99e472f0d0" "answer-eb90fc15-7950-575d-a8ff-31fa8bd25ec6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83e83f58-9225-53a6-8e6a-f42f69406481" :answer/id #uuid "83e83f58-9225-53a6-8e6a-f42f69406481" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be58a7fb-a086-5860-ad30-dd1c817fbd59" :answer/id #uuid "be58a7fb-a086-5860-ad30-dd1c817fbd59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51f5ec9c-cf1f-5d72-a5d8-f8dc65eacd30" :answer/id #uuid "51f5ec9c-cf1f-5d72-a5d8-f8dc65eacd30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dac76dc6-a248-5bf4-bc16-bc99e472f0d0" :answer/id #uuid "dac76dc6-a248-5bf4-bc16-bc99e472f0d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb90fc15-7950-575d-a8ff-31fa8bd25ec6" :answer/id #uuid "eb90fc15-7950-575d-a8ff-31fa8bd25ec6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d724ae77-2273-56ab-852e-2415e473e7f8" :question/id #uuid "d724ae77-2273-56ab-852e-2415e473e7f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-13840" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2}{5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | ${e}^{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2}{5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{2}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5e5e2b78-7327-5ca0-90fb-487bdfff6019"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5e5e2b78-7327-5ca0-90fb-487bdfff6019" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5e2b78-7327-5ca0-90fb-487bdfff6019" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d0c5c72a-52a6-527f-9089-d3942f82a598" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74dd2751-1a10-5b13-a07e-4a1b5ceee5f6" "answer-d0c5c72a-52a6-527f-9089-d3942f82a598" "answer-fa48eb2e-b23d-5975-8ee4-2650534bd1bf" "answer-53d5b4d4-65c5-534f-b5bf-9a4d54b10bf5" "answer-4403caea-cd74-51a9-b79d-725521c1723f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74dd2751-1a10-5b13-a07e-4a1b5ceee5f6" :answer/id #uuid "74dd2751-1a10-5b13-a07e-4a1b5ceee5f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0c5c72a-52a6-527f-9089-d3942f82a598" :answer/id #uuid "d0c5c72a-52a6-527f-9089-d3942f82a598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa48eb2e-b23d-5975-8ee4-2650534bd1bf" :answer/id #uuid "fa48eb2e-b23d-5975-8ee4-2650534bd1bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53d5b4d4-65c5-534f-b5bf-9a4d54b10bf5" :answer/id #uuid "53d5b4d4-65c5-534f-b5bf-9a4d54b10bf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4403caea-cd74-51a9-b79d-725521c1723f" :answer/id #uuid "4403caea-cd74-51a9-b79d-725521c1723f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101535 :question/problem "What is the value of ${\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{x{log}_{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{x{log}_{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{log}_{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =4{ln}^{2}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100371 :answer-field/correct "answer-13a0a75b-f8ec-54c5-8a7a-c4809a5dfbd1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64a568b0-03ae-50f3-9960-f6a12c2c3edd" "answer-13a0a75b-f8ec-54c5-8a7a-c4809a5dfbd1" "answer-e68587f4-8c6a-5209-a952-e474e449105e" "answer-8351c1fb-1f5f-531e-b8d0-f8d53498e7df" "answer-9773d021-d3dc-5a4f-a413-83c7aabfc9ac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64a568b0-03ae-50f3-9960-f6a12c2c3edd" :answer/id #uuid "64a568b0-03ae-50f3-9960-f6a12c2c3edd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13a0a75b-f8ec-54c5-8a7a-c4809a5dfbd1" :answer/id #uuid "13a0a75b-f8ec-54c5-8a7a-c4809a5dfbd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{ln}^{2}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e68587f4-8c6a-5209-a952-e474e449105e" :answer/id #uuid "e68587f4-8c6a-5209-a952-e474e449105e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8351c1fb-1f5f-531e-b8d0-f8d53498e7df" :answer/id #uuid "8351c1fb-1f5f-531e-b8d0-f8d53498e7df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡2}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9773d021-d3dc-5a4f-a413-83c7aabfc9ac" :answer/id #uuid "9773d021-d3dc-5a4f-a413-83c7aabfc9ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186320609 :answer-field/correct "answer-0444227a-dd50-5fbc-9b4c-b746cc7ac5e4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0444227a-dd50-5fbc-9b4c-b746cc7ac5e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0444227a-dd50-5fbc-9b4c-b746cc7ac5e4" :answer/id #uuid "0444227a-dd50-5fbc-9b4c-b746cc7ac5e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\ln 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186102029 :tutorial/content "Let's think about how to calculate an integral like $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {\\ln x} {x} \\,\\textrm d x.$\n\nNotice that this integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac {\\ln x} {x} \\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\underbrace{\\ln x}_{u} \\cdot\\overbrace{\\dfrac {1} {x}}^{u'} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe've seen integrals like this before, where the integrand consists of a function $u(x)$ multiplied by its derivative $u'(x).$ Such integrals can be solved by substitution.\n\nSo, we let $u = \\ln x,$ which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad   \\Longrightarrow \\quad \\dfrac 1 x \\,\\textrm{d}x={\\textrm{d}u}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we can calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       \\int \\dfrac{\\ln x}{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \t&=\\int \\ln x\\cdot \\dfrac {1} {x} \\,\\textrm d x \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t& = \\int u \\, \\textrm{d} u \\[5pt]\n                                                                &=  \\dfrac{1}{2}u^2  +C \\[5pt]   \n                                                                &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\ln^2 x +C}\n$$\n\nAfter solving an integral using substitution, we should always double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({ln}^{2}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186102030 :tutorial/content "Let's evaluate the following definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^4} \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }\n$$\n\nWe'll use the change of variable method, which comprises three steps:\n\n**Step 1:**  Change the variable.\n\nLet's introduce the new variable $u = \\ln x.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{x}\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\textrm{d}u = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2:**  Find the new limits of integration.\n\nWe use the table below to change our limits of integration from $x$ to $u{:}$\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\n**Step 3:** Evaluate the integral in the new variable $u.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{u}^{1/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6(\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =6(2-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101029 :activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
